{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. Blood pressure's one thirty six over eighty two, pulse seventy four, temp thirty six point four, oxygen ninety eight percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thanks sister. Right, what's today about?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Hip.",
  "[SEG0004] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ja, the check-up. Traffic was hectic at the robot, hey. Six weeks since the right hip replacement.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right hip still sore when you walk far?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (PATIENT): Bit.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ag, parking this side was a proper nightmare.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Stiff?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Err, Dad's still stiff in that hip. Started last winter, or the one before, I can't pin which.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any ooze from the wound?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Calf swollen?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me look. Wound's healed, dry, no redness this side. Steady enough on the stick.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Still on the asprin?",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ja, by mouth every morning for the clots, since the op. Umm I nearly said twenty milligrams, ag no, it's a hundred milligrams.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): And a painkiller?",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Panado, paracetemol. Five hundred milligrams, two tablets by mouth when the hip nags. Not every day.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Righto. Sister, bloods Thursday morning, eight o'clock. Full blood count and a CRP. No starving. Asprin as usual that morning.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (NURSE): Sharp. Thursday at eight, I'll take them. No fasting.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll see you in two weeks. If that CRP is borderline we do an x-ray. If the hip has not settled by then, a scan.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Must he keep the stick?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Keep the stick. Don't stop the asprin till I say. Looks like straightforward recovery, nothing to suggest a clot.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Shame, he'll be glad. My dad stays with me, so transport's easy.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): Ja."
 ],
